# ADVANCED-EDITION-CODE: in the advanced edition's build, never the standard one's.
#
# The advanced settings window's own sources: what its build compiles after every source
# gui/window.sources names, one repository-relative path per line, in the order csc is given
# them, under the one group `[advanced]`.
#
# The standard window is gui/window.sources and nothing else, and its build never reads this
# file, so a type declared in a source listed here cannot reach the standard executable. No
# source of the standard window names one either (advanced/tests/test_advanced_package.py).
#
# The Dashboard's Advanced features page, which joins the standard window through the `partial void`
# points gui/Dashboard.cs declares (DashboardBuilt, SnapshotApplied, PendingBuilt), its Keep it on and Send
# now cards (v0.6.14), its watch log - what a watched capability would have done (v0.6.14) - the reset
# actions' rules on it and on Pending (v0.6.14), the compatibility report's card on it, and the page's own
# audit - and (v0.6.15-beta) keep going's card, and the prompt queue's on it and on Pending - and (v0.6.16-beta.4) the
# near-the-limit choices with the wrap-up's own wordings, and the turns run here, each with its Stop - and (v0.6.16)
# the page in the render mode the documentation's pictures are drawn in - and (v0.6.19, #50) the prompt queue's editor and
# Pending's Recoveries | Scheduled tabs.

[advanced]
advanced/gui/AdvancedPage.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedKeepOn.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedWatch.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedResets.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedKeepGoing.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedQueue.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedEditor.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedSchedule.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedReport.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedUsage.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedRuns.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedPageAudit.cs
advanced/gui/AdvancedRender.cs
